# LF in every checkout, whatever core.autocrlf says. A Windows clone with
# the Git-for-Windows default (autocrlf=true) otherwise gets CRLF, and the
# files that run inside Linux containers break: docker/db/init/*.sh dies on
# `/bin/bash^M` and leaves the database unhealthy, Caddy and psql read the
# CR into their input, and pnpm refuses the patches. Prettier and
# .editorconfig already ask for LF; this makes the checkout agree with them.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Byte for byte as committed, never converted: a patch's hunks must match
# the upstream file exactly, and vue-i18n ships dist/vue-i18n.d.ts with CRLF,
# so those CRs belong in the patch.
patches/*.patch -text
